Build Sabra Job Engine V1 core: M1-M7 with live-verified discovery and ranking

Implements the canonical build contract in SABRA_JOB_ENGINE_V1_BUILD.md from
scaffolding to a working loop, verified against real data.

What works, with evidence
- M2 Discovery: 23 real ATS boards (22 Greenhouse, 1 Lever) read through their public
  JSON APIs -> 1,126 postings normalized into 1,098 canonical opportunities. A repeat
  run is fully idempotent (0 new, 1,126 unchanged).
- M3 Intelligence: 1,094 opportunities screened -> 25 qualified -> 10 shortlisted,
  led by genuine medical-device field-sales roles. Rejections are recorded with
  reasons and remain in history.
- M4 Application factory: truth-bound tailoring that selects and reorders
  candidate-authored content, never paraphrasing it. Every generated line is
  traceable, and verify_tailored_truth is tested to fail on a fabricated bullet.
- M5 Approval: approval carries the content hash of the package a human read; the
  execution path recomputes it and refuses on any difference.
- M6 Execution: a Playwright adapter written against a real captured Greenhouse form
  (51 fields). The live form is CAPTCHA-protected, so the adapter detects and stops
  rather than working around it, per requirement 21.
- M7 Ledger: append-only events, the requirement-22 ledger projection, outcomes and
  the requirement-25 learning records.

Layering
packages/domain (models, schema, state machines, repositories, event log),
packages/llm (provider abstraction, null by default), packages/providers
(Greenhouse, Lever, direct careers; normalization; deduplication),
packages/scoring (features, hard filter, fit, ranking), packages/documents
(master resume, tailoring, answers, packages), packages/automation (adapter
contract, Greenhouse adapter), packages/engine (services and CLI).

172 tests passing. The deterministic path needs no model configured; every reasoning
feature has a fallback and SABRA_LLM_PROVIDER defaults to none.

Defects found by real data, not by the suite
- ASCII-only title normalization collapsed every CJK title to "", merging unrelated
  postings into one opportunity.
- Deduplication merged on title+location alone, collapsing two roles that described
  different territories into one opening.
- Geography compared raw tokens, so a posting reading "Texas" never matched a profile
  reading "TX".
- Candidate skills were extracted but never merged into the evidence the scorers read,
  so a skills-heavy profile scored zero qualification coverage.
- Function-word n-grams let "Director of Bioinformatics" match "Director of Sales".
- Hand-quoted CSS selectors produced a JavaScript syntax error, caught only by driving
  a real browser.
- The submission path moved APPROVED to APPLIED directly, which the state machine
  forbids: a successful submission would have raised after the employer received it.
  State moves now derive their route from the transition graph.

Not built / not verified
- No FastAPI app and no web UI yet.
- The PostgreSQL path is documented and dialect-agnostic but has NOT been executed;
  Docker is unavailable on this machine, so the pilot runs on SQLite.
- M8 is blocked on owner input: package generation correctly refuses to invent
  candidate facts, so with no resume loaded it produces INCOMPLETE packages naming
  every open question.

Assumptions and the full defect register: docs/architecture/assumptions.md.
